---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import { availableSubjects, subjectsUnderDevelopment } from '../data/availableSubjects';
import { subjectCategories } from '../data/subjectCategories';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const categories = subjectCategories.map((category) => ({
  ...category,
  subjects: availableSubjects.filter((subject) => subject.category === category.id)
})).filter((category) => category.subjects.length > 0);
const subjectCatalogCount = availableSubjects.length + subjectsUnderDevelopment.length;
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Subjects, Classes & Learning Resources | Study Hub"
  description={`Explore Study Hub's ${availableSubjects.length} currently available subject libraries, class levels, notes, past papers, and teaching resources.`}
>
  <main class="subjects-directory">
    <header class="directory-intro guide-hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">Study Hub · Learning guide</p>
      <h1>Find the right resources for your learning journey.</h1>
      <p>
        Study Hub brings school learning resources together in one searchable library: choose a class,
        explore an available subject, and find notes, exam papers, and teaching materials where they
        are available.
      </p>
      <div class="guide-stats" aria-label="Current subject availability">
        <div><strong>{availableSubjects.length}</strong><span>subjects available now</span></div>
        <div><strong>{subjectCatalogCount}</strong><span>subjects in the catalog</span></div>
        <div><strong>{subjectsUnderDevelopment.length}</strong><span>being prepared</span></div>
      </div>
      <nav class="guide-actions" aria-label="Subject guide actions">
        <a class="guide-primary-link" href="#available-subjects">Explore available subjects <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        <a href={`${base}/library.html`}>Browse the library</a>
      </nav>
      <p class="guide-availability-note">
        Catalog totals describe subject pages, not the number of individual files. Only subjects
        marked available below have a live public subject page; preparation is not a promise of a
        launch date.
      </p>
    </header>

    <nav class="guide-toc" aria-label="On this page">
      <a href="#how-it-works">How Study Hub works</a>
      <a href="#classes-levels">Classes &amp; levels</a>
      <a href="#resources">Resource types</a>
      <a href="#available-subjects">Available subjects</a>
      <a href="#university">University learning</a>
      <a href="#using-resources">Using resources well</a>
    </nav>

    <section class="guide-section" id="how-it-works" aria-labelledby="how-it-works-heading">
      <div class="guide-section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">01 · The service</p>
        <h2 id="how-it-works-heading">A library for learners and educators</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        Study Hub helps learners find revision material and gives teachers and other educators a
        place to discover useful classroom resources. Browse by class or subject, search descriptive
        details, then open a resource in the document reader. The Study Assistant can also help
        explain a topic, but it is a study aid rather than an official source or a replacement for
        teaching.
      </p>
      <div class="guide-feature-grid">
        <article class="guide-feature">
          <span class="guide-feature-number">01</span>
          <h3>Choose where you are studying</h3>
          <p>Start with a class shelf or go directly to one of the public subject libraries.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="guide-feature">
          <span class="guide-feature-number">02</span>
          <h3>Find a useful resource</h3>
          <p>Look for notes, papers, guides, and other materials using the available search and filters.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="guide-feature">
          <span class="guide-feature-number">03</span>
          <h3>Study and check your understanding</h3>
          <p>Read at your own pace, practise with questions, and verify important information with your teacher.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-section" id="classes-levels" aria-labelledby="classes-levels-heading">
      <div class="guide-section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">02 · Learning stages</p>
        <h2 id="classes-levels-heading">Classes and levels</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        The library’s class shelves are arranged to help you browse from early learning through
        primary and secondary school. The current class browser includes:
      </p>
      <div class="guide-level-grid">
        <article><h3>Early childhood</h3><p>Baby Class, Middle Class, and Top Class.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Primary</h3><p>Primary 1 through Primary 7 (P.1–P.7).</p></article>
        <article><h3>O-Level · lower secondary</h3><p>Senior 1 through Senior 4 (S.1–S.4).</p></article>
        <article><h3>A-Level · upper secondary</h3><p>Senior 5 and Senior 6 (S.5–S.6).</p></article>
      </div>
      <p class="guide-callout">
        Class shelves describe how the library is organised; they do not mean that every subject or
        class already has a complete collection. Subject pages currently cover O-Level and A-Level
        materials for the four available subjects. Check each resource’s details and level before
        using it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-section" id="resources" aria-labelledby="resources-heading">
      <div class="guide-section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">03 · What you can find</p>
        <h2 id="resources-heading">Papers, notes, and teaching materials</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        Resources are added and described over time. What appears depends on the subject, class,
        source, and material currently available; use the library search and the details on each
        item to confirm it suits your needs.
      </p>
      <div class="guide-resource-list">
        <article>
          <h3>Past and practice papers</h3>
          <p>Use examination papers and practice questions to revisit topics, practise timing, and identify what to study next. Check the level, year, and examination source when those details are shown.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>Subject notes and study guides</h3>
          <p>Review explanations and topic-based material alongside your class notes and current course guidance.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>Teachers’ guides</h3>
          <p>Where published, teaching guides can support lesson preparation and help educators explore approaches to a subject.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>Schemes of work</h3>
          <p>Where available, schemes of work can help with planning topics across a period. Always compare a scheme with your school’s calendar, syllabus, and current teacher guidance.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>Other learning materials</h3>
          <p>The library may also include reference documents and supplementary resources. Resource labels and descriptions can vary by source.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p class="guide-callout">
        A resource being listed does not mean it is an official, complete, or current syllabus.
        Follow your school’s programme and the latest guidance from your teacher or examining body.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-section" id="available-subjects" aria-labelledby="available-subjects-heading">
      <div class="guide-section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">04 · Public subject libraries</p>
        <h2 id="available-subjects-heading">{availableSubjects.length} subjects available now</h2>
        <p>
          These are the subject pages currently published with a resource library. Subject coverage
          and file availability can differ by level and topic.
        </p>
      </div>

      <section class="directory-controls" aria-label="Filter available subjects">
        <label class="directory-search-label" for="subject-search">Search available subjects</label>
        <input id="subject-search" type="search" placeholder="Search subjects..." autocomplete="off" data-subject-search />
        <div class="category-filters" role="group" aria-label="Subject category filters">
          <button type="button" class="category-filter is-active" data-category-filter="all" aria-pressed="true">
            All <span>{availableSubjects.length}</span>
          </button>
          {categories.map((category) => (
            <button type="button" class="category-filter" data-category-filter={category.id} aria-pressed="false">
              {category.filterLabel} <span>{category.subjects.length}</span>
            </button>
          ))}
        </div>
        <p class="directory-result-count" data-result-count aria-live="polite">Showing {availableSubjects.length} subjects</p>
      </section>

      <nav class="directory-jump-nav" aria-label="Jump to subject category">
        {categories.map((category) => (
          <a href={`#${category.id}`}>{category.label}</a>
        ))}
      </nav>

      <div class="directory-groups">
        {categories.map((category) => (
          <section class="directory-category" id={category.id} data-category-section={category.id} aria-labelledby={`${category.id}-heading`}>
            <div class="directory-category-heading">
              <div>
                <p class="eyebrow">{category.filterLabel}</p>
                <h3 id={`${category.id}-heading`}>{category.label}</h3>
              </div>
              <p>{category.description}</p>
            </div>
            <div class="directory-subject-grid">
              {category.subjects.map((subject) => (
                <article
                  class="directory-subject"
                  data-subject-card
                  data-category={category.id}
                  data-search={`${subject.name} ${subject.focus} ${subject.description} ${subject.tracks.join(' ')}`.toLowerCase()}
                >
                  <span class="directory-subject-icon" aria-hidden="true">{subject.icon}</span>
                  <div>
                    <h4><a href={`${base}/frontend/src/html/${subject.slug}.html`}>{subject.name}</a></h4>
                    <p>{subject.description}</p>
                    <span class="directory-subject-levels">{subject.tracks.join(' · ')}</span>
                  </div>
                </article>
              ))}
            </div>
          </section>
        ))}
        <p class="directory-no-results" data-no-results hidden>No available subjects match that search. Try another term or category.</p>
      </div>
      <p class="directory-development-note">
        The full catalog also lists {subjectsUnderDevelopment.length} subjects being prepared. They
        are not public subject libraries yet. <a href={`${base}/under-development.html`}>See the current development list</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-section guide-university" id="university" aria-labelledby="university-heading">
      <div class="guide-section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">05 · Future expansion</p>
        <h2 id="university-heading">University learning is planned</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        Study Hub is planning to expand beyond school resources to include university-level work.
        University materials are not yet part of the public subject catalog. As this collection is
        developed, it can be organised around programmes and courses, year or semester, topic, and
        resource type so that students can find relevant material without mixing it up with
        school-level content.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you have a university subject or type of resource you would like prioritised, <a href={`${base}/community-chat.html`}>send a suggestion</a>.
        Please share only material you have permission to distribute.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-section" id="using-resources" aria-labelledby="using-resources-heading">
      <div class="guide-section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">06 · Study responsibly</p>
        <h2 id="using-resources-heading">Make the most of each resource</h2>
      </div>
      <ol class="guide-checklist">
        <li><strong>Check the context.</strong> Confirm the subject, class or level, year, and source where those details are available.</li>
        <li><strong>Use papers for practice.</strong> Attempt questions before checking solutions, and review mistakes against your class notes.</li>
        <li><strong>Compare teaching materials.</strong> Adapt guides and schemes to the syllabus and schedule followed by your school.</li>
        <li><strong>Verify important information.</strong> Resources can differ in date, format, and completeness; ask your teacher when something is unclear.</li>
        <li><strong>Use AI thoughtfully.</strong> Treat generated explanations as study support, check them against trusted materials, and do not submit personal or confidential information.</li>
      </ol>
      <div class="guide-end-links">
        <a class="guide-primary-link" href={`${base}/library.html`}>Open the library <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        <a href={`${base}/documentation.html`}>Read the site documentation</a>
        <a href={`${base}/privacy.html`}>Review the privacy policy</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <script>
    const searchInput = document.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-subject-search]');
    const filterButtons = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-category-filter]'));
    const subjectCards = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-subject-card]'));
    const categorySections = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-category-section]'));
    const resultCount = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-result-count]');
    const noResults = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-no-results]');

    let activeCategory = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search).get('category') || 'all';
    if (!filterButtons.some((button) => button.dataset.categoryFilter === activeCategory)) activeCategory = 'all';

    function updateSubjectList() {
      const query = searchInput?.value.trim().toLocaleLowerCase() || '';
      let visibleCount = 0;

      for (const card of subjectCards) {
        const categoryMatches = activeCategory === 'all' || card.dataset.category === activeCategory;
        const searchMatches = !query || (card.dataset.search || '').includes(query);
        card.hidden = !(categoryMatches && searchMatches);
        if (!card.hidden) visibleCount += 1;
      }

      for (const section of categorySections) {
        section.hidden = !section.querySelector('[data-subject-card]:not([hidden])');
      }

      if (resultCount) resultCount.textContent = `Showing ${visibleCount} subject${visibleCount === 1 ? '' : 's'}`;
      if (noResults) noResults.hidden = visibleCount > 0;
      for (const button of filterButtons) {
        const isActive = button.dataset.categoryFilter === activeCategory;
        button.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(isActive));
        button.classList.toggle('is-active', isActive);
      }
    }

    for (const button of filterButtons) {
      button.addEventListener('click', () => {
        activeCategory = button.dataset.categoryFilter || 'all';
        updateSubjectList();
      });
    }

    searchInput?.addEventListener('input', updateSubjectList);
    updateSubjectList();
  </script>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
  .guide-hero {
    padding: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
    border: 1px solid #d8ded5;
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #fffefa 0%, #f3f7f1 100%);
  }

  .guide-hero h1 {
    max-width: 18ch;
    font-family: Manrope, sans-serif;
    font-size: clamp(2.15rem, 5vw, 3.6rem);
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
  }

  .guide-hero > p:not(.eyebrow) {
    max-width: 68ch;
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .guide-stats {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0;
    margin-top: 2rem;
    border: 1px solid #d8ded5;
    background: rgba(255, 254, 250, .8);
  }

  .guide-stats > div {
    display: grid;
    min-width: 150px;
    gap: 3px;
    padding: 14px 20px;
    border-right: 1px solid #d8ded5;
  }

  .guide-stats > div:last-child { border-right: 0; }
  .guide-stats strong { color: #246b49; font: 800 1.5rem/1.1 Manrope, sans-serif; }
  .guide-stats span { color: #617068; font-size: .75rem; }

  .guide-actions, .guide-end-links {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 12px 20px;
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
  }

  .guide-actions a, .guide-end-links a {
    color: #285c3e;
    font-size: .86rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .guide-actions .guide-primary-link, .guide-end-links .guide-primary-link {
    display: inline-flex;
    min-height: 44px;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 9px;
    padding: 0 16px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    background: #246b49;
    color: #fffefa;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .guide-availability-note { color: #718078 !important; font-size: .78rem !important; }

  .guide-toc {
    position: sticky;
    z-index: 5;
    top: 0;
    display: flex;
    gap: 4px;
    margin: 0 -4px;
    padding: 10px 4px;
    overflow-x: auto;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #d8ded5;
    background: rgba(244, 245, 239, .97);
    scrollbar-width: thin;
  }

  .guide-toc a {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    padding: 7px 10px;
    color: #435b4b;
    font-size: .76rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-decoration: none;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .guide-toc a:hover, .guide-toc a:focus-visible { color: #246b49; text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }

  .guide-section {
    padding: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem) 0;
    scroll-margin-top: 64px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #d8ded5;
  }

  .guide-section > p, .guide-section-heading > p:last-child {
    max-width: 78ch;
    color: #53645a;
    font-size: .94rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .guide-section-heading { margin-bottom: 18px; }
  .guide-section-heading .eyebrow { margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .guide-section-heading h2 { margin: 0; color: #293b32; font: 800 clamp(1.45rem, 3vw, 2rem)/1.2 Manrope, sans-serif; }
  .guide-feature-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); margin-top: 22px; border: 1px solid #d8ded5; background: #fffefa; }
  .guide-feature { padding: 22px; border-right: 1px solid #d8ded5; }
  .guide-feature:last-child { border-right: 0; }
  .guide-feature-number { color: #246b49; font: 800 .7rem/1 Manrope, sans-serif; letter-spacing: .12em; }
  .guide-feature h3, .guide-level-grid h3, .guide-resource-list h3 { margin: 12px 0 7px; color: #293b32; font: 700 1rem/1.35 Manrope, sans-serif; }
  .guide-feature p, .guide-level-grid p, .guide-resource-list p { margin: 0; color: #617068; font-size: .82rem; line-height: 1.65; }
  .guide-level-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); margin-top: 20px; border-top: 1px solid #d8ded5; border-left: 1px solid #d8ded5; background: #fffefa; }
  .guide-level-grid article { padding: 18px; border-right: 1px solid #d8ded5; border-bottom: 1px solid #d8ded5; }
  .guide-level-grid h3 { margin-top: 0; }
  .guide-resource-list { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); margin-top: 20px; border-top: 1px solid #d8ded5; border-left: 1px solid #d8ded5; background: #fffefa; }
  .guide-resource-list article { padding: 20px; border-right: 1px solid #d8ded5; border-bottom: 1px solid #d8ded5; }
  .guide-resource-list h3 { margin-top: 0; }
  .guide-callout { margin-top: 20px; padding: 16px 18px; border-left: 3px solid #6b9478; background: #edf4ec; color: #435b4b !important; }
  .guide-checklist { display: grid; gap: 12px; max-width: 80ch; padding-left: 22px; color: #53645a; font-size: .9rem; line-height: 1.7; }
  .guide-checklist li::marker { color: #246b49; font-weight: 800; }
  .guide-checklist strong { color: #293b32; }
  .guide-university { padding-inline: clamp(1.25rem, 4vw, 2rem); border: 1px solid #d8ded5; border-top: 3px solid #6b9478; background: #fffefa; }
  .guide-university + .guide-section { border-top: 0; }
  .directory-development-note { margin-top: 20px; padding: 16px; background: #f0f5ef; color: #53645a; font-size: .86rem; line-height: 1.65; }
  .directory-development-note a { color: #285c3e; font-weight: 700; }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .guide-feature-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .guide-feature { border-right: 0; border-bottom: 1px solid #d8ded5; }
    .guide-feature:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
    .guide-stats > div { flex: 1 1 40%; }
    .guide-stats > div:nth-child(2) { border-right: 0; }
    .guide-stats > div:last-child { border-top: 1px solid #d8ded5; }
  }

  @media (max-width: 520px) {
    .guide-level-grid, .guide-resource-list { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .guide-stats > div { min-width: 0; padding: 12px; }
  }
</style>
